# Target tree

This directory is where the agent will land the TypeScript surface and the Go
core (under `native/`). Crane creates files here during iterations — they should
not exist before the first iteration.

The evaluator expects a driver at one of:
- `run_case.mjs`  (run with `node`)
- `run_case.js`   (run with `node`)
- `run_case.ts`   (run with `bun`)

The driver reads one parity case as JSON on stdin and prints the result as JSON
on stdout. See `../../evaluate.py` for the contract.
